And if I'm a parent, what should I look for to know that my child may be developing and eating? disorder and it's not just a phase, as you said. There's a lot of things that parents can look for. So the number one most important thing is any sort of changes in eating habits. This is why we know that family meals can be so protective against eating disorders because parents are there to observe and notice if kids are starting to eat differently. So if all of a sudden your kid isn't finishing their food or all they want to start cutting out a food group. Maybe they decide to be vegetarian or vegan, but it's not really

