have better coverage. If you look at, for example, the mental health parity laws, and each of the states have a rating for how well they do mental health disparity from A to F. So, you know, everybody wants an A. Nobody wants an F. Well, I think it's something like 47 states get an F and like two states have a D minus and one has a D. So, so I, so I, so I, I mean, the point is, is that we're not doing well when it comes to mental health parity. And that's not just eating disorders, that everything. Yeah. Right.

